 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is also published in machine-readable form at a second route — a supported surface that returns the same veterinarians `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Either surface can be narrowed to the veterinarians holding one named specialty: given a specialty, the page shows only those veterinarians, with pagination applying to the narrowed list, and the machine-readable surface returns only those veterinarians `[REQ-VET-003]`. The specialty is matched on its whole name, ignoring letter case — not as a prefix. A specialty no veterinarian holds yields the ordinary page or document with an empty veterinarian list, not an error, and a blank or all-spaces specialty behaves as though it were not given at all — the same way an empty owner search behaves `[REQ-VET-003]`. Without a specialty, both surfaces list every veterinarian as before `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty, when the machine-readable surface is opened, then it returns the same veterinarians the page lists.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty one or more veterinarians hold, when the page is opened with it, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty, when the machine-readable surface is opened with it, then only the veterinarians holding it are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a value differing from a held specialty only by letter case, when either surface is opened with it, then it matches; given a value that is only a prefix of a held specialty, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when either surface is opened with it, then the ordinary page or document is returned with an empty veterinarian list and a success status.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a blank or all-spaces specialty, when either surface is opened with it, then the result matches the same surface opened with no specialty.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. The machine-readable surface and the page draw from the same veterinarians, so a specialty filter yields the same set on both. This second route was formerly recorded here as a defect — an unconsumed machine-readable list carrying no requirement — and now carries `REQ-VET-003` as a supported surface. The withdrawn `REQ-VET-002` on the Superseded list is unchanged and its ID is not reused.
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
